cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this forecast or its code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "2026 U.S. House, Senate and governor forecast"
abstract: >-
  A daily Monte Carlo forecast of the 2026 U.S. House, Senate and governor elections that blends each race's polls with a
  fundamentals prior and simulates the elections with correlated national, state, regional and race errors, run in
  GitHub Actions.
authors:
  - family-names: Corvec
    given-names: Shawn
repository-code: "https://github.com/scorvec/midterms-2026"
url: "https://scorvec.com/midterms"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-10-16
keywords:
  - elections
  - election forecasting
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - polling
  - U.S. House
  - U.S. Senate
